From 39c18877e042e13156849b861d07bc3c92e64db4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett Heap <1513478+brettheap@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:41:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The spec leg gets its own front door: the shape's leg
 AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and README.md, the LF rule and licence it lost when the
 root kept them, and the claude-current manual's three test paths re-pointed
 at the code leg.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rehearsal patch for opensoft/openRepoTools#186, task T006 of
specs/004-migrate-to-triad/tasks.md, against run C's spec leg 593250d. The
split left this leg with no AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md, LICENSE or
.gitattributes, because all of them stayed in the assembly root, and a
superproject's attributes never reach into a submodule's worktree.

- AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and README.md are openRepoShape 7f84ca4's
  templates/spec-root/ files, rendered by its own copy_tree with this
  project's names, so the leg-clone detector in scripts/shape_advisory.py
  recognises them. Each AGENTS.md and README.md then adds one short section:
  what this leg holds; that full proposals and canonical Speckit files live
  here, and a bounded amendment in the code leg's feature folder; where
  `openspec validate` runs; and how to read a pre-split path or commit hash.
- .gitattributes restores the `* text=auto eol=lf` rule the monorepo's root
  file applied to these documents. `git add --renormalize .` changes nothing.
- LICENSE is the root's Apache-2.0 text, byte for byte (blob 261eeb9).
- docs/README-claude-current.md:275-276: `tests/test_claude_current.py`,
  `tests/test_claude_restart_check.py` and
  `tests/test_lane_start_claude_current.py` become `code/tests/…`, relative
  to the assembly root.

No approval record is rewritten. Paths and commit hashes recorded in
openspec/changes/ and specs/ are left as their authors wrote them, under
FR-014 of specs/004-migrate-to-triad/spec.md. docs/README-lanes.md is left
to the lane-tooling analysis.

Lane: openRepoTools-1
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
